{
 "id": "V013-VS-08-prune",
 "note": "0.1.3 version skew (lib/plugver.pm), load records stay bounded: a process's first start prunes .sessions/loads/ at most once a day (loads/.pruned). Kept: the record of a process that runs (the runner's own here, by the seam-fed process table STORE_TEST_PROC_STARTS; its process may start another session), the newest record per version and scope (0.1.0, 0.1.1, 0.1.3 of the user scope; 0.1.2 of another scope tag), and the newest records of the last 7 days (at most 200); dropped: older ones and a record dated a day ahead. More drops than the batch (3 here, STORE_TEST_LOADS_BATCH; 500 by default) move the folder aside to .sessions/loads-drop/<epoch>-<pid> with the kept ones moved back, so a reader at once lists a small folder; each later first start drains at most a batch of the oldest moved folder, and a record dated from a minute before its move goes back to loads/. /clear and compaction starts (no record written) do neither. 0.1.4 (V-2, V-3, V-6): a record counts as its process's only while its pid runs with the start time its name holds (a reused pid's record goes; a pid whose start cannot be read counts as running), and at most $KEEP_MAX of them are kept (2 here, STORE_TEST_LOADS_KEEP); another machine's record (its machine id differs) is kept while it is from the last 7 days, whatever runs here, and dropped after; a loads/.pruned dated an hour ahead does not stop the prune.",
